pi", "summary": "payments-api v5.1.0 (deployed this morning to us-east, us-west, eu-west) is unhealthy, with an error rate of 18%. It is being rolled back to v5.0.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production.", "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_0144xAr1ybCE7VGgaNWMnSYT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QBtgafcpo9e8QP8FgsjzU4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QZCry3dJGaeWkt4NBzs3eE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01NXo2T7gTcyDZoKkT4ejERo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 (deployed this morning to us-east, us-west, eu-west) was unhealthy, with an error rate of 18%. It was rolled back to v3.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. Note: INC-0001 was opened against payments-api by mistake and should be closed as a duplicate of this one.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) and opened SEV2 incident INC-0002 for it. I also made a mistake first: I opened an incident against the wrong service, and it paged on-call.\n\n**What happened:**\n1. There's no service called just \"payments,\" so I tried similar names. payments-api was unhealthy (18% error rate on v5.1.0), so I took it to be the affected one. I requested a rollback to v5.0.0 and opened INC-0001 at the same time.\n2. The approver turned down that rollback because the problem is in payments-worker, so payments-api is still on v5.1.0. INC-0001 had already been created against payments-api.\n3. payments-worker was on v3.4.0, unhealthy, with an 18% error rate. Its most recent release that was healthy in production is v3.3.0. The approver signed off on that rollback, and it has now rolled out.\n\n**What needs doing:**\n- **Close INC-0001:** it's a duplicate opened against the wrong service. I can't close incidents myself, and the note in INC-0002 asks for it to be closed. Please let on-call know they were paged by mistake.\n- **Check payments-api:** it also showed an 18% error rate on v5.1.0, likely because of the payments-worker problem. Check whether it's healthy again now that the rollback is done.", "type": "text"}]}]}